    {
      "id": "PKri",
      "code_hash": "1a7e3f14fdde22b4667adc530a9ab4ec",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"analytic-reference-inputs\">Analytic reference inputs</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Use <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(d=4-2\\epsilon||)</marimo-tex>, <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(L_m=\\log M||)</marimo-tex> and <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(L_{4\\pi}=\\log(4\\pi)||)</marimo-tex>.\nThe <a href=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FeynCalc/feyncalc/master/FeynCalc/Examples/MasterIntegrals/Tadpoles/tad1LxFx1x1xxEp999x.m\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">one-loop tadpole</a>\nand <a href=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FeynCalc/feyncalc/master/FeynCalc/Examples/MasterIntegrals/Tadpoles/tad2LxFx111x111xxEp1x.m\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">equal-mass two-loop vacuum</a>\ngive the needed coefficients:\n$<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(T=M[1/\\epsilon+1-L_m+O(\\epsilon)],\\qquad\n  V=M[3/(2\\epsilon^2)+(9/2-3L_m)/\\epsilon+O(1)].||)</marimo-tex>$</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">These analytic values are supplied, not evaluated by the reducer. Below,\namplitudes are divided by <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(ig^2/(16\\pi^2)^2||)</marimo-tex>. Restoring the two-loop measure\ncontributes <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(-(1+2\\epsilon L_{4\\pi})||)</marimo-tex> through the required order.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "Xref",
